  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 309 PM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nIn the wake of the exiting system Friday night, Saturday will \nfeature chance pops, although forecast QPF will be light at \nbest. Northeasterly winds, and cloud cover will limit highs to \nthe upper 60s to middle 70s for most areas. By Saturday night \npersistent upper level low pressure will approach western, then \ncentral Wyoming by 12z Sunday. A lead disturbance, will lead to \na decent chance for precipitation Saturday night into Sunday \nmorning. ATTM the greatest threat appears across western into \nsouthwestern portions of the forecast area. The upper level low \nwill migrate from central Wyoming into South Dakota Sunday into \nSunday night bringing another threat for showers and \nthunderstorms to the forecast area. As this system exits into \nthe upper Mississippi Valley Monday, a second low and trough of \nlow pressure aloft, will lift from southern California into the \nintermountain west Tuesday. Downstream of this feature, there \nwill be a continued chance for showers and thunderstorms Monday \nthrough Wednesday. The trough is progged to clear the forecast \narea Wednesday night with lower precipitation chances expected \nfor Thursday. Highs early next week will be in the 60s, with a \nreturn to 70s mid week.",
